### Changes in this version (8.0.0) since 7.5.1

#### New features:
 - [%as:]: added support for 'default' keyword as a filter option to result program
 - [%as:]: added db_name param to Firestore_job_database
 - [%as:]: switched reports to using human_method_type property from alignment classes
 - [%as:]: added ability to specify alignment method on the command line
 - [%as:]: job q program now limits from the most recent jobs, not the oldest
 - [%as:]: unavailable nodes are now hidden by default
 - [%as:]: stopped creating double licenses for cloud only sign-ups
 - [%as:]: added hubspot email functionality to stripe endpoint
 - [%as:]: added customer deleted endpoint
 - [%as:]: also listen for subscription cancel events
 - [%as:]: enabled update_subscription endpoint
 - [%as:]: added update_subscription endpoint
 - [%as:]: added missing background-tasks
 - [%as:]: added further endpoints for stripe
 - [%as:]: added initial version of stripe endpoint
 - [%as:]: added initial versions of stripe endpoints
 - [%as:]: added better error reporting when lacking policy permissions
 - [%as:]: added support for multiple license policies and restricting access based on policy
 - [%as:]: updated programs to use bundled binaries as defaults
 - [%as:]: updated authorship info
 - [%as:]: updated to new digilib/digichem structure
 - [%as:]: enabled authentication for v0 api
 - [%as:]: migrated store_in_db and poll_interval options
 - [%as:]: migrated structure from calculation to destination
 - [%as:]: migrated scratch options from calculation objects to destination objects
 - [%as:]: updated build-static to latest xTB versions
 - [%as:]: CREST, CENSO, xtb, xtb4stda, and std2 now use the pre-compiled digichem binaries by default
 - [%as:]: added build-static files as sub-module
 - [%as:]: increased xTB density cube step-size to 0.5
 - [%as:]: removed the broken GFN0-xTB method
 - [%as:]: added OMP_NUM_THREADS to slurm templates to cover numpy and other libs loading openmp too early for us to change threads
 - [%as:]: enabled density fitting by default on most PySCF calculations
 - [%as:]: disabled opt/freq combined jobs for PySCF as density fitting is poorly supported here
 - [%as:]: permitted some method fields to be set in api submissions
 - [%as:]: added library_path options for xTB, xtb4stda, and std2
 - [%as:]: improved logging support for xTB and other programs that print info to stderr
 - [%as:]: xtb now only writes density.cube files if a report has bene requested
 - [%as:]: PySCF now supports ECPs
 - [%as:]: added better clean-up options for xTB and PySCF with sTDA
 - [%as:]: updated sTD-DFT calculations for PySCF to reduce number of orbitals and set function exchange
 - [%as:]: pyscf now passes std2_log_file to parse if one exists
 - [%as:]: added std2_log_file_path property to Std2_mixin
 - [%as:]: added support for calculating sTDA states with pyscf wavefunction
 - [%as:]: increased step size for xtb density plots
 - [%as:]: xtb excited states now only render HOMO+3 to LUMO-3
 - [%as:]: added support for xTB excited states
 - [%as:]: added ability to render total density for xTB
 - [%as:]: added ability to write xTB xcontrol
 - [%as:]: initial calc definitions for xTB
 - [%as:]: added support for generating images with xTB
 - [%as:]: added initial support for xTB
 - [%as:]: reduced general api access level to just USER, set submission endpoints as LICENSE
 - [%as:]: profiling steps can now be given in decimals
 - [%as:]: added option to toggle the slow spin-dipole interaction in PySCF NMR coupling
 - [%as:]: license update is now run as a background task
 - [%as:]: updated envs
 - [%as:]: added function to auto update licenses
 - [%as:]: expanded digichemd to support env
 - [%as:]: switched default PySCF geometry solver to geometric
 - [%as:]: set local methods to hidden
 - [%as:]: added error reporting when trying to submit a method that does not exist
 - [%as:]: adjusted API for jobs to better include relationships
 - [%as:]: added support for submitting matrices with IDs & overrides
 - [%as:]: added initial support for supplying overrides for library methods

#### Bugfixes:
 - [%as:]: PySCF now properly supports scf['iterations']
 - [%as:]: fixed tinyDB IDs missing initial zero characters
 - [%as:]: fixed library path arguments sometimes getting mangled when edited in the terminal interface
 - [%as:]: fixed get_node_children endpoint
 - [%as:]: fixed Turbomole calculations not applying SCS paramaters correctly
 - [%as:]: fixed Turbomole calculations not placing some temp files in the scratch location
 - [%as:]: fixed not being able to specify scs params for Turbomole
 - [%as:]: fixed typo in report resulting in wrong style for fractions
 - [%as:]: the same
